"zkMatrix: Batched Short Proof for Committed Matrix Multiplication (https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/161)\nciteturn3view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view0\",\"lineno\":29}); Total lines: 77\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of cite0†tin foil†iacr.org ?\nL2: \nL3: cite1†Cryptology ePrint Archive L4: \nL5:   * cite2†Papers Updates from the last:\nL6:     * cite3†7 days L7:     * cite4†31 days L8:     * cite5†6 months L9:     * cite6†365 days L10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * cite7†Listing by year L13:     * cite8†All papers L14:     * cite9†Compact view L15:     * cite10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org L16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * cite11†How to cite L19:     * * * *\nL20:     * cite12†Harvesting metadata L21:   * cite2†Submissions L22:     * cite13†Submit a paper L23:     * cite14†Revise or withdraw a paper L24:     * cite15†Acceptance and publishing conditions L25: \nL26: cite16†Image: Search Button L27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2024/161\nL30: \nL31: ### cite17†zkMatrix: Batched Short Proof for Committed Matrix Multiplication L32: \nL33: Mingshu Cong, University of Hong Kong\nL34: \nL35: Tsz Hon Yuen, Monash University\nL36: \nL37: Siu Ming Yiu, University of Hong Kong\nL38: ##### Abstract\nL39: Matrix multiplication is a common operation in applications like machine learning and data analytics. To demonstrate the correctness of such an operation in a privacy-preserving manner, we propose zkMatrix, a zero-knowledge proof for the multiplication of committed matrices.\nL40: Among the succinct non-interactive zero-knowledge protocols that have an $O(\\log n)$ transcript size and $O(\\log n)$ verifier time, zkMatrix stands out as the first to achieve $O(n^2)$ prover time and $O(n^2)$ RAM usage for multiplying two $n \\times n$ matrices. Significantly, zkMatrix distinguishes itself as the first zk-SNARK protocol specifically designed for matrix multiplication.\nL41: By batching multiple proofs together, each additional matrix multiplication only necessitates $O(n)$ group operations in prover time.\nL42: ##### Metadata\nL43: \nL44: Available format(s)\nL45:     cite17†PDF L46: Category\nL47:     cite18†Cryptographic protocols L48: Publication info\nL49:     Published elsewhere. AsiaCCS 2024\nL50: Keywords\nL51:     cite19†zero-knowledge proof cite20†matrix multiplication cite21†zk-SNARK L52: Contact author(s)\nL53:     mscong @ cs hku hk\nL54: john tszhonyuen @ monash edu\nL55: smyiu @ cs hku hk\nL56: History\nL57:     2024-02-07: last of 2 revisions\nL58:     2024-02-04: received\nL59:     cite22†See all versions L60: Short URL\nL61:     cite23†https://ia.cr/2024/161†ia.cr L62: License\nL63: \nL64: cite24†CC BY†creativecommons.org L65: BibTeX cite25†Image Copy to clipboard\nL66: \nL67:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2024/161,\nL68:           author = {Mingshu Cong and Tsz Hon Yuen and Siu Ming Yiu},\nL69:           title = {{zkMatrix}: Batched Short Proof for Committed Matrix Multiplication},\nL70:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2024/161},\nL71:           year = {2024},\nL72:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/161}\nL73:     }\nL74: \nL75: \nL76: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease Release v4.0.0 · ingonyama-zk/icicle · GitHub (https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/releases/tag/v4.0.0)\nciteturn3view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view1\",\"lineno\":185}); Total lines: 269\nL113: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115: cite61†ingonyama-zk / cite62†icicle Public\nL116: \nL117:   * cite63†Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL118:   * cite63†Fork 171 L119:   * cite63†Star L120:   * cite64†Code L121:   * cite65†Issues 27 L122:   * cite66†Pull requests 22 L123:   * cite67†Actions L124:   * cite68†Projects L125:   * cite69†Security and quality 0 L126:   * cite70†Insights L127: \nL128: Additional navigation options\nL129: # Release v4.0.0\nL130: \nL131: cite71†Latest L132: \nL133: Compare\nL134: \nL135: # Choose a tag to compare\nL136: \nL137: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL138: \nL139: Filter\nL140: \nL141: Loading [Input]\nL142: \nL143: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL144: \nL145: ### Uh oh!\nL146: \nL147: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL148: \nL149: ## No results found\nL150: \nL151: cite72†View all tags L152: \nL153: cite73†Image: @github-actions†avatars.githubusercontent.com cite74†github-actions released this 11 Jul 05:36\nL154: \nL155: · cite75†13 commits to main since this release\nL156: \nL157: cite64†v4.0.0 L158: \nL159: cite76†`6c77775` L160: \nL161: # ICICLE v4.0.0 Release Notes\nL162: ## 🎉 Major Release: ICICLE v4.0.0\nL163: \nL164: We're excited to announce the release of ICICLE v4.0.0! This major version introduces significant improvements to the API design, making it more intuitive, object-oriented, and developer-friendly across all supported languages.\nL165: ## 🚀 Key Highlights\nL166:   * Object-Oriented Field API: Complete redesign of field operations from static methods to instance methods\nL167:   * Method Chaining Support: Write more concise and expressive code with method chaining\nL168:   * Improved Rust API: Better trait design with standard operator overloading\nL169:   * Enhanced Program API: Reorganized Program module with better type safety\nL170:   * Backward Compatibility: Comprehensive migration guides for v3 to v4 transition\nL171:   * Post Quantum: Implemented a NIST FIPS203 (ML-KEM) protocol on CUDA, fully open-source\nL172:   * Lattice Based Cryptography: Add support for Lattice based cryptography, with integer ring support and a full LaBRADOR prover (soon announced)\nL173: ## 🔄 Breaking Changes\nL174: \nL175: ### C++ API Changes\nL176: \nL177: #### Field Arithmetic Operations\nL178: \nL179: All field operations have been converted from static methods to instance methods\nL180: Check the cite77†migration page†dev.ingonyama.com for more details\nL181: \nL182: ### Rust API Changes\nL183: \nL184: #### Arithmetic Trait Redesign\nL185: \nL186: The `FieldImpl` trait has been deprecated and split into focused, orthogonal traits\nL187: ## What's Changed\nL188:   * Negacyclic NTT for polynomial rings by cite78†@yshekel in cite79†#930 L189:   * Update README.md by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite81†#931 L190:   * Fixed devdocs link licensing by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite82†#933 L191:   * Fix collab instructions for version mismatch error by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite84†#935 L192:   * Feat: generate JL-projection matrix rows by cite78†@yshekel in cite85†#936 L193:   * Curve Montgomery Conversion Fix for Host Memory by cite86†@emirsoyturk in cite87†#938 L194:   * [FIX] Invalid memory access causes hang by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite88†#939 L195:   * PQC ML-KEM by cite89†@nonam3e and cite90†@dorshmil in cite91†#932 L196:   * Add PQC documentation to 3.9.0 by cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite93†#940 L197:   * Changed broken link on readme by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite94†#942 L198:   * [FEAT] Rust Polynomial-Ring trait and NegacyclicNTT by cite78†@yshekel in cite95†#943 L199:   * [FEAT] Decompose Polynomial-rings by cite78†@yshekel in cite96†#945 L200:   * [FEAT] JL-projection Rust wrapper by cite78†@yshekel in cite97†#949 L201:   * [FEAT] MatMul API by cite98†@lnm-at-work in cite99†#871 L202:   * [FEAT] Expose Sumcheck protocol challenge vector by cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite100†#946 L203:   * Timur/pqc go wrappers by cite89†@nonam3e in cite101†#944 L204:   * [FEAT] Add flattening utilities for polynomial slices into scalar slices by cite78†@yshekel in cite102†#952 L205:   * [CI] Separate testing by feature by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite103†#913 L206:   * [FEAT] Add reinterpretation utilities and polynomial vector operations by cite78†@yshekel in cite104†#954 L207:   * [FIX] typo in ci.yml by cite78†@yshekel in cite105†#959 L208:   * [REFACTOR] move matrix transpose to matrix_ops, add PolyRing support and tests by cite78†@yshekel in cite106†#961 L209:   * [CI] Fix Go tests and Rust bn254 by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite107†#960 L210:   * [CI] Move merkle test to hash crate by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite108†#963 L211:   * Determine the scalar size according to configuration if provided by cite109†@mickeyasa in cite110†#955 L212:   * [FEATURE] Pseudorandom field element sampling from seed by cite111†@ChickenLover in cite112†#950 L213:   * Validate JL projection consistency across backends by cite90†@dorshmil in cite113†#956 L214:   * devdocs: June 15 Update by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite114†#947 L215:   * consistent norm check by cite86†@emirsoyturk in cite115†#967 L216:   * Devdocs quick fix by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite116†#969 L217:   * [FIX] fix int devision bug in MSM by cite117†@idanfr-ingo in cite118†#970 L218:   * [Feat] matrix ops rust by cite98†@lnm-at-work in cite119†#957 L219:   * [FIX] Matmul rust wrappers identify device memory and assert sizes by cite78†@yshekel in cite120†#977 L220:   * [FIX] Unify Zq and Rq Balanced Base-b Decomposition Using Digit-Major Layout by cite78†@yshekel in cite121†#979 L221:   * [FIX] Replace `dependent_option` with regular `option` by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite122†#976 L222:   * [FEATURE] Add matrix transpose support to Rust matrix_ops wrapper by cite78†@yshekel in cite123†#984 L223:   * Add manual trigger for full test suite by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite124†#987 L224:   * Feat/challenge space sampling by cite111†@ChickenLover in cite125†#966 L225:   * fix random sampling small size bug by cite111†@ChickenLover in cite126†#994 L226:   * Relax norm bound API: support size > 2¹⁶ and full-range L∞ values by cite78†@yshekel in cite127†#998 L227:   * [FEAT] Allow disabling features from rust bindings by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite128†#978 L228:   * V4 Rust wrapper redesign by cite111†@ChickenLover , cite89†@nonam3e , cite129†@vhnatyk , cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite130†#990 L229:   * ICICLE V4 by cite111†@ChickenLover , cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite131†#982 L230:   * [Feat] matmul + transpose fusion by cite98†@lnm-at-work in cite132†#1000 L231:   * [EXAMPLE] Add Rust example showcasing icicle-lattice APIs by cite78†@yshekel in cite133†#965 L232:   * [FIX] compilation for arm by cite78†@yshekel in cite134†#1001 L233:   * Some more changes to devdocs by cite80†@Shalmoni in cite135†#981 L234:   * ICICLE V4 documentation update by cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite136†#999 L235:   * [FIX] Enable and fix examples by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite137†#972 L236:   * Update release workflow to use examples as reusable workflow by cite83†@jeremyfelder in cite138†#1004 L237:   * Remove `-q` from Rust examples to show output by cite78†@yshekel in cite139†#1003 L238:   * Rename labrador to babykoala by cite78†@yshekel in cite140†#1005 L239:   * Fix lattice-snark example import by cite92†@LeonHibnik in cite141†#1006 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nicicle/LICENSE at main · ingonyama-zk/icicle · GitHub (https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/blob/main/LICENSE)\nciteturn3view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks